I don’t think that plot suggests underestimation of total abundance per se. If you’re worried about total abundance, I would look at the observed vs predicted total count (i.e., the sum of the counts across all of your samples) or possibly observed vs predicted max counts.

The plot you shared shows that you are under-predicting small counts and over-predicting larger counts, which I think can be interpreted as suggesting that the population is more spread out across the landscape than estimated by the model. Zero-inflation might help somewhat with this, but I suspect not entirely as zero-inflation will help shore up the zeros but not necessarily the ones. I actually have been finding similar patterns of lack of fit with count-based abundance models I’ve been working on recently, which makes me wonder if this is typical of these models.

